lisa-selfreview:
Pass 1 of 1 (lenient), verdict approve. One finding fixed before the commit, none left.
Fixed: CORE-DUP-001 (should-fix) the harness and lending blocks install.sh writes copy agent.yaml.example's; TestInstallScriptDryRun now parses both with the agent's loader and requires them equal, so they can't drift. Also fixed during verification: errorlint (errors.As on the ExitError) and shellcheck SC2154.
Checked: CORE-SEC-001/003 (the enrollment and claude tokens are read with read -rs from /dev/tty or the env, written 0600 under umask 077, never printed or put in argv: printf is a builtin; FACTORY_VERSION, the dispatcher, pool and host are validated before they reach a URL or the YAML); CORE-INPUT-001 (an existing agent.yaml or token file is never overwritten; SHA256SUMS must hold an exact line for each asset and match, else it refuses); CORE-TEST-001/002 (dry runs for darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 and --no-service, refusals for other platforms, --yes without values and a bad version; fail-loud stubs for curl, install, mkdir, launchctl, systemctl, loginctl, sudo, tart, shasum, sha256sum and factory-agent, and HOME must stay empty; a mutation of the driver or the harness block fails the test); CORE-VERIFY-001 (make -k reviewable: only the known macOS TestBaseScriptRuns; release-assets now ships install.sh and SHA256SUMS verifies it).
Design: the config also carries host (so the printed enroll command names the same host the agent registers as), harnesses and lending: the loader refuses a config without at least one harness and a lending block, so the brief's three keys alone wouldn't load. supervise runs as the owner in both services (supervise.md: the workspaces are the user's; kata's root actions go through sudo -n kata-helper), so Linux gets a systemd user unit, plus a loginctl enable-linger hint. Logins are offered only interactively; --yes leaves them for later and prints the commands.
